# Sidecar binaries directory: track placeholder stubs, ignore real PyInstaller artefacts.
# Real binaries are large PyInstaller bundles (700+ MB) — they are replaced during
# the release workflow and must never be committed (GitHub blocks >100 MB blobs).
# The placeholder stubs (shell scripts) ARE committed so that `cargo check` succeeds
# on every platform without a real build.
#
# Because the binary paths are already tracked as stubs, .gitignore alone cannot
# prevent the real binaries from being staged when locally rebuilt — gitignore
# only suppresses *untracked* files. The robust protection is:
#   git update-index --skip-worktree src-tauri/binaries/jura-sidecar-<triple>
# applied once per developer machine after the first local sidecar build. This
# tells git to ignore local modifications to the stub even though it is tracked.
# CI does not need this because each runner starts fresh from the stub.
#
# Convention: a real binary is larger than 1 MB; a placeholder stub is a few bytes.

# CLIP ONNX exports mirrored into the Tauri bundle dir at build time
# (parallel to the canonical models/clip-vit-b32-* rule below). ~580 MB
# combined; sourced from models/ during bundling, never committed.
src-tauri/models/clip-vit-b32-vision.onnx
src-tauri/models/clip-vit-b32-vision.onnx.data
src-tauri/models/clip-vit-b32-text.onnx
src-tauri/models/clip-vit-b32-text.onnx.data


